id: pm-starter-puy5
title: Measure all executable pm-starter TypeScript and statement coverage
description: "The current release coverage gate reports 100% lines, branches and functions over three files, while the docstring gate sees six authored TypeScript files. Node V8 coverage does not report statements separately, so 100/100/100/100 cannot be claimed. Executable scripts/main-invocation.ts, scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts and scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts need explicit inventory and direct behavior coverage, with any type-only exclusion justified."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:quality",coverage-scope
created_at: "2026-09-29T14:51:25.166Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T22:49:11.894Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Inventory all six authored executable TypeScript source files and prove which the current gate omits; coverage gate fails when any authored executable source is unmeasured; measure statements lines branches functions at 100% per included file with real tests; retain docstring and release gate parity without artificial exclusions or duplicated tests.; Use instrumentation that separately reports statements before claiming four measured dimensions at 100 percent. The current V8 lines/branches/functions report cannot satisfy that prerequisite
risk: medium
confidence: high
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T22:48:40.644Z",codex-sol,"Cubic correctly identifies the current V8 metric limitation, already recorded in this issue. Keep the four-dimension 100 percent requirement: changing it to three dimensions would weaken the requested acceptance. Added an explicit instrumentation prerequisite so it is future work, not an impossible claim about the present gate. No threshold, test scope or quality gate changed."
body: ""
